{"advice_coverage":{"additional_concern_fix_plans":3,"additional_concerns":3,"finding_assessment_slots":2,"finding_assessments":2,"finding_fix_plans":2,"interpretation":"Fix plans are proposals, not executed patches or validated safeguards. Finding/check assessment counts include actual model answers only; synthesized omitted slots are separate. Missing model advice remains absent; static guidance stays available.","model_check_assessments":0,"model_check_fix_plans":0,"omitted_finding_assessments":0,"static_findings":11,"static_fix_plans":11},"analyst":{"enabled":false},"assessment":{"coverage_attention":[],"finding_groups":[{"confidence_counts":{"medium":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["EXEC-02"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["AGT-01","AUTH-02","MCP-02"],"how_it_helps":"Have an execution service allow only named operations, permitted argument values, and caller-owned target resources before invoking a tool.","id":"tool-policy","residual_limit":"Authorized operations can still be harmful when business constraints are incomplete; prompt instructions cannot enforce this boundary.","source_ids":["OWASP-AGENT-CS","MCP-TOOLS"],"sources":[{"id":"MCP-TOOLS","title":"MCP: Tools","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"},{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Enforce action policy outside the model","verification":"Exercise disallowed operations, additional arguments, cross-tenant identifiers, and direct calls that bypass the agent planner."},{"control_ids":["EXEC-02","SUP-05","OPS-02"],"how_it_helps":"Run the risky tool in a separate, disposable identity with no host mounts, ambient credentials, or unnecessary outbound access.","id":"execution-isolation","residual_limit":"Isolation limits reachable assets; it does not make injected code trustworthy or rule out a runtime escape.","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Isolate tool execution","verification":"In a test environment, attempt reads outside the workspace, forbidden network connections, and resource exhaustion; retain policy and denial evidence."}],"finding_ids":["b1b0f0a3f33fe93875fcb58a"],"id":"group-45290f4fa5c7","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Trace the input to eval/exec and replace it with fixed operations; if generated execution is essential, isolate it before accepting untrusted input.","locations":[{"end_line":16,"finding_id":"b1b0f0a3f33fe93875fcb58a","line":16,"path":"agent.py"}],"plausible_impact":"If external or generated content reaches this expression, it could execute Python with the process identity and access its files, credentials, and network.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI001","severity":"high","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY","MCP-TOOLS","OWASP-AGENT-CS","OWASP-LLM2026","TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"MCP-TOOLS","title":"MCP: Tools","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"},{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"},{"id":"OWASP-LLM2026","title":"OWASP GenAI LLM Top 10 2026","url":"https://genai.owasp.org/resource/owasp-genai-llm-top-10-2026/"},{"id":"TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY","title":"Python Security Considerations","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/security_warnings.html"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Agent/tool developer","title":"Dynamic Python code execution"},{"confidence_counts":{"medium":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["EXEC-01"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["AGT-01","AUTH-02","MCP-02"],"how_it_helps":"Have an execution service allow only named operations, permitted argument values, and caller-owned target resources before invoking a tool.","id":"tool-policy","residual_limit":"Authorized operations can still be harmful when business constraints are incomplete; prompt instructions cannot enforce this boundary.","source_ids":["OWASP-AGENT-CS","MCP-TOOLS"],"sources":[{"id":"MCP-TOOLS","title":"MCP: Tools","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"},{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Enforce action policy outside the model","verification":"Exercise disallowed operations, additional arguments, cross-tenant identifiers, and direct calls that bypass the agent planner."},{"control_ids":["EXEC-02","SUP-05","OPS-02"],"how_it_helps":"Run the risky tool in a separate, disposable identity with no host mounts, ambient credentials, or unnecessary outbound access.","id":"execution-isolation","residual_limit":"Isolation limits reachable assets; it does not make injected code trustworthy or rule out a runtime escape.","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Isolate tool execution","verification":"In a test environment, attempt reads outside the workspace, forbidden network connections, and resource exhaustion; retain policy and denial evidence."}],"finding_ids":["979d192981c1785a2394fe19"],"id":"group-66e04ed7d9ac","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Remove shell interpretation, select a fixed executable, and validate each argument and permitted option.","locations":[{"end_line":9,"finding_id":"979d192981c1785a2394fe19","line":9,"path":"agent.py"}],"plausible_impact":"If a caller or agent controls command content, shell syntax could alter the intended operation and execute with the tool process permissions.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI002","severity":"high","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY","MCP-TOOLS","OWASP-AGENT-CS","OWASP-LLM2026","OWASP-MCP10","OWASP-OUTPUT2025","TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"MCP-TOOLS","title":"MCP: Tools","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"},{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"},{"id":"OWASP-LLM2026","title":"OWASP GenAI LLM Top 10 2026","url":"https://genai.owasp.org/resource/owasp-genai-llm-top-10-2026/"},{"id":"OWASP-MCP10","title":"OWASP MCP Top 10","url":"https://owasp.org/projects/mcp-top-10"},{"id":"OWASP-OUTPUT2025","title":"LLM05:2025 Improper Output Handling","url":"https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm052025-improper-output-handling/"},{"id":"TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY","title":"Python Security Considerations","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/security_warnings.html"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Agent/tool developer","title":"Dynamic command executed through a shell"},{"confidence_counts":{"medium":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["EXEC-01"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["AGT-01","AUTH-02","MCP-02"],"how_it_helps":"Have an execution service allow only named operations, permitted argument values, and caller-owned target resources before invoking a tool.","id":"tool-policy","residual_limit":"Authorized operations can still be harmful when business constraints are incomplete; prompt instructions cannot enforce this boundary.","source_ids":["OWASP-AGENT-CS","MCP-TOOLS"],"sources":[{"id":"MCP-TOOLS","title":"MCP: Tools","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"},{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Enforce action policy outside the model","verification":"Exercise disallowed operations, additional arguments, cross-tenant identifiers, and direct calls that bypass the agent planner."},{"control_ids":["EXEC-02","SUP-05","OPS-02"],"how_it_helps":"Run the risky tool in a separate, disposable identity with no host mounts, ambient credentials, or unnecessary outbound access.","id":"execution-isolation","residual_limit":"Isolation limits reachable assets; it does not make injected code trustworthy or rule out a runtime escape.","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Isolate tool execution","verification":"In a test environment, attempt reads outside the workspace, forbidden network connections, and resource exhaustion; retain policy and denial evidence."}],"finding_ids":["0fa7e450cd583d78646ef397"],"id":"group-f0e53150bfd5","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Replace os.system/os.popen with a fixed executable and validated argument list; trace all contributing values.","locations":[{"end_line":10,"finding_id":"0fa7e450cd583d78646ef397","line":10,"path":"agent.py"}],"plausible_impact":"If external values contribute to the command string, the shell could execute additional commands with the server identity.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI003","severity":"high","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY","MCP-TOOLS","OWASP-AGENT-CS","OWASP-LLM2026","OWASP-MCP10","OWASP-OUTPUT2025","TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"MCP-TOOLS","title":"MCP: Tools","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"},{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"},{"id":"OWASP-LLM2026","title":"OWASP GenAI LLM Top 10 2026","url":"https://genai.owasp.org/resource/owasp-genai-llm-top-10-2026/"},{"id":"OWASP-MCP10","title":"OWASP MCP Top 10","url":"https://owasp.org/projects/mcp-top-10"},{"id":"OWASP-OUTPUT2025","title":"LLM05:2025 Improper Output Handling","url":"https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm052025-improper-output-handling/"},{"id":"TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY","title":"Python Security Considerations","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/security_warnings.html"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Agent/tool developer","title":"Dynamic os shell command"},{"confidence_counts":{"medium":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["EXEC-06"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["SUP-03","DATA-04"],"how_it_helps":"Require reviewed artifact provenance plus a digest or signature checked against an independently trusted identity or manifest.","id":"artifact-verification","residual_limit":"Authenticity establishes the producer and bytes; an approved producer can still ship vulnerable or malicious content.","source_ids":["SLSA-12","OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING"],"sources":[{"id":"OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","title":"Launch of Model Signing v1.0","url":"https://openssf.org/blog/2025/04/04/launch-of-model-signing-v1-0-openssf-ai-ml-working-group-secures-the-machine-learning-supply-chain/"},{"id":"SLSA-12","title":"Supply-chain Levels for Software Artifacts specification","url":"https://slsa.dev/spec/v1.2/"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Verify artifact identity before use","verification":"Substitute bytes, producer identity, or verification metadata in a controlled test and confirm the consumer rejects the artifact."},{"control_ids":["EXEC-06","SUP-06"],"how_it_helps":"Perform necessary conversion of legacy serialized artifacts in a disposable environment without production data or credentials.","id":"isolated-conversion","residual_limit":"Conversion output still needs integrity, format, and downstream behavior review; isolation is not proof of benign content.","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY","TECH-PYTORCH-SERIAL"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"TECH-PYTORCH-SERIAL","title":"PyTorch Serialization semantics","url":"https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/notes/serialization.html"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Separate artifact conversion from production","verification":"Demonstrate that a conversion job cannot reach production services and only approved output formats are promoted."}],"finding_ids":["d2d09fb2875db72f18779bfc"],"id":"group-9ee5075ce1a1","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Establish who can produce and replace the input; migrate to a nonexecutable data format or restrict verified legacy artifacts to an isolated conversion path.","locations":[{"end_line":12,"finding_id":"d2d09fb2875db72f18779bfc","line":12,"path":"agent.py"}],"plausible_impact":"If an attacker can supply or replace the serialized input, loading it may execute code even before the application examines the returned object.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI005","severity":"high","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY","NIST-SSDF","OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","SLSA-12","TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY","TECH-PYTORCH-SERIAL"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"NIST-SSDF","title":"Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1","url":"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final"},{"id":"OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","title":"Launch of Model Signing v1.0","url":"https://openssf.org/blog/2025/04/04/launch-of-model-signing-v1-0-openssf-ai-ml-working-group-secures-the-machine-learning-supply-chain/"},{"id":"SLSA-12","title":"Supply-chain Levels for Software Artifacts specification","url":"https://slsa.dev/spec/v1.2/"},{"id":"TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY","title":"Python Security Considerations","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/security_warnings.html"},{"id":"TECH-PYTORCH-SERIAL","title":"PyTorch Serialization semantics","url":"https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/notes/serialization.html"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Application/model pipeline owner","title":"Executable deserialization requires trusted inputs"},{"confidence_counts":{"high":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["MCP-01"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["MCP-01","AUTH-05"],"how_it_helps":"Use verified TLS on every relevant network hop, with an appropriate public or private CA and validated service hostname.","id":"trusted-transport","residual_limit":"TLS does not protect data from an authorized endpoint, compromised gateway, or plaintext segments beyond termination.","source_ids":["MCP-AUTH","MCP-AUTH-SEC"],"sources":[{"id":"MCP-AUTH","title":"MCP: Authorization","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH-SEC","title":"MCP: Authorization Security Considerations","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization/security-considerations"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Require authenticated encrypted transport","verification":"Present an untrusted, expired, or wrong-host certificate and verify rejection; inspect backend traffic after TLS termination."},{"control_ids":["EXEC-05","AGT-07","SUP-05"],"how_it_helps":"Enforce an outbound policy outside the application that permits only required destinations and services; include IPv6 and proxy paths.","id":"egress-policy","residual_limit":"Allowed destinations may themselves accept leaked data; destination rules do not replace content and action authorization.","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY","MCP-SECURITY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"MCP-SECURITY","title":"MCP Security Best Practices","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Restrict outbound destinations independently","verification":"From the deployed identity, test direct IP, DNS, redirect, metadata-service, and proxy-mediated attempts to prohibited destinations."}],"finding_ids":["07fc5f6fd7699fd0194dc479"],"id":"group-08a6f7f32c94","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Enable certificate and hostname verification; install the intended CA for a private gateway and test rejection of an untrusted certificate.","locations":[{"end_line":11,"finding_id":"07fc5f6fd7699fd0194dc479","line":11,"path":"agent.py"}],"plausible_impact":"If a network intermediary can impersonate the destination, disabled verification may expose or alter credentials, prompts, and tool responses.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI006","severity":"high","source_ids":["CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","JOINT-DEPLOY","MCP-AUTH","MCP-AUTH-SEC","MCP-HTTP","MCP-SECURITY"],"sources":[{"id":"CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","title":"Shifting the Balance of Cybersecurity Risk: Principles and Approaches for Secure by Design Software","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/secure-by-design"},{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH","title":"MCP: Authorization","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH-SEC","title":"MCP: Authorization Security Considerations","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization/security-considerations"},{"id":"MCP-HTTP","title":"MCP: Streamable HTTP transport","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/streamable-http"},{"id":"MCP-SECURITY","title":"MCP Security Best Practices","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Application and gateway owner","title":"TLS certificate verification disabled"},{"confidence_counts":{"medium":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["AUTH-05","DATA-01"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["AUTH-05","OPS-06"],"how_it_helps":"For a real exposed credential, identify reachable systems, revoke or rotate it, and review access records for misuse.","id":"exposure-response","residual_limit":"Successful rotation stops future use of that credential but cannot reverse access or data loss that already occurred.","source_ids":["CISA-JCDC","NIST-SSDF"],"sources":[{"id":"CISA-JCDC","title":"JCDC AI Cybersecurity Collaboration Playbook and Fact Sheet (release notice)","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/alerts/2025/01/14/cisa-releases-jcdc-ai-cybersecurity-collaboration-playbook-and-fact-sheet"},{"id":"NIST-SSDF","title":"Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1","url":"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Investigate and contain confirmed secret exposure","verification":"Confirm the old credential no longer works and record the exposure window, affected copies, and follow-up owner."},{"control_ids":["AUTH-05","DATA-01","DATA-06"],"how_it_helps":"Load secrets at runtime through an approved store or workload identity; keep them out of source, artifacts, and model context.","id":"credential-lifecycle","residual_limit":"Deleting a file or hiding a later image layer does not revoke a credential or erase copies already distributed.","source_ids":["MCP-AUTH","JOINT-AGENTIC"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH","title":"MCP: Authorization","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Use managed credential injection and revocation","verification":"Test rotation and revocation without disclosing values; inspect build layers and launch metadata for retained copies."},{"control_ids":["AUTH-05","AUTH-09"],"how_it_helps":"Give this component a distinct identity and only the downstream scopes and lifetime needed for its approved operations.","id":"secret-boundary","residual_limit":"A compromised component can still use its allowed permissions until credentials expire or revocation takes effect.","source_ids":["JOINT-AGENTIC"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Limit credentials available to the workload","verification":"Use its runtime identity to attempt forbidden service operations, then revoke it and confirm subsequent access fails."}],"finding_ids":["afb2bdb94696690028650faf"],"id":"group-57a1992f928c","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Determine whether the value is real without reproducing it; revoke or rotate a real exposed credential and remove retained copies through the incident process.","locations":[{"end_line":6,"finding_id":"afb2bdb94696690028650faf","line":6,"path":"mcp.json"}],"plausible_impact":"If the detected literal is a live credential, anyone with access to the source, image layers, or copied artifacts may use its granted permissions.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI010","severity":"high","source_ids":["CISA-JCDC","CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","JOINT-AGENTIC","JOINT-DEPLOY","MCP-AUTH","MCP-AUTH-SEC","MCP-SECURITY","NIST-SSDF"],"sources":[{"id":"CISA-JCDC","title":"JCDC AI Cybersecurity Collaboration Playbook and Fact Sheet (release notice)","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/alerts/2025/01/14/cisa-releases-jcdc-ai-cybersecurity-collaboration-playbook-and-fact-sheet"},{"id":"CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","title":"Shifting the Balance of Cybersecurity Risk: Principles and Approaches for Secure by Design Software","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/secure-by-design"},{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"},{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH","title":"MCP: Authorization","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH-SEC","title":"MCP: Authorization Security Considerations","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization/security-considerations"},{"id":"MCP-SECURITY","title":"MCP Security Best Practices","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices"},{"id":"NIST-SSDF","title":"Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1","url":"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Credential/service owner","title":"Credential-like literal in source or configuration"},{"confidence_counts":{"high":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["MCP-01"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["MCP-01","AUTH-05"],"how_it_helps":"Use verified TLS on every relevant network hop, with an appropriate public or private CA and validated service hostname.","id":"trusted-transport","residual_limit":"TLS does not protect data from an authorized endpoint, compromised gateway, or plaintext segments beyond termination.","source_ids":["MCP-AUTH","MCP-AUTH-SEC"],"sources":[{"id":"MCP-AUTH","title":"MCP: Authorization","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH-SEC","title":"MCP: Authorization Security Considerations","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization/security-considerations"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Require authenticated encrypted transport","verification":"Present an untrusted, expired, or wrong-host certificate and verify rejection; inspect backend traffic after TLS termination."},{"control_ids":["AUTH-05","AUTH-09"],"how_it_helps":"Give this component a distinct identity and only the downstream scopes and lifetime needed for its approved operations.","id":"secret-boundary","residual_limit":"A compromised component can still use its allowed permissions until credentials expire or revocation takes effect.","source_ids":["JOINT-AGENTIC"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Limit credentials available to the workload","verification":"Use its runtime identity to attempt forbidden service operations, then revoke it and confirm subsequent access fails."}],"finding_ids":["d841174f55e032505f8136b9"],"id":"group-b69c379f05c4","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Use HTTPS with verified certificates; if a separate protected transport is intentional, document and test every network hop and termination boundary.","locations":[{"end_line":10,"finding_id":"d841174f55e032505f8136b9","line":10,"path":"mcp.json"}],"plausible_impact":"If remote traffic traverses an unprotected link, observers or intermediaries may read or modify MCP credentials, requests, and responses.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI029","severity":"high","source_ids":["JOINT-AGENTIC","MCP-AUTH","MCP-AUTH-SEC","MCP-HTTP","MCP-SECURITY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH","title":"MCP: Authorization","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH-SEC","title":"MCP: Authorization Security Considerations","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization/security-considerations"},{"id":"MCP-HTTP","title":"MCP: Streamable HTTP transport","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/streamable-http"},{"id":"MCP-SECURITY","title":"MCP Security Best Practices","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"MCP/gateway owner","title":"Remote MCP URL uses plaintext HTTP"},{"confidence_counts":{"high":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["AGT-01","AGT-02","MCP-09","SUP-05"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["AGT-01","AUTH-02","MCP-02"],"how_it_helps":"Have an execution service allow only named operations, permitted argument values, and caller-owned target resources before invoking a tool.","id":"tool-policy","residual_limit":"Authorized operations can still be harmful when business constraints are incomplete; prompt instructions cannot enforce this boundary.","source_ids":["OWASP-AGENT-CS","MCP-TOOLS"],"sources":[{"id":"MCP-TOOLS","title":"MCP: Tools","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"},{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Enforce action policy outside the model","verification":"Exercise disallowed operations, additional arguments, cross-tenant identifiers, and direct calls that bypass the agent planner."},{"control_ids":["AGT-02","OPS-04"],"how_it_helps":"Require an independent approval for the exact actor, tool, normalized arguments, target, and expiry before irreversible effects occur.","id":"action-approval","residual_limit":"Approval cannot compensate for misleading previews, excessive approver authority, or actions that happen before the check.","source_ids":["OWASP-AGENT-CS"],"sources":[{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Bind sensitive actions to explicit approval","verification":"Change arguments after approval, replay the approval, and call after expiry; each attempt must be denied before a side effect."},{"control_ids":["EXEC-02","SUP-05","OPS-02"],"how_it_helps":"Run the risky tool in a separate, disposable identity with no host mounts, ambient credentials, or unnecessary outbound access.","id":"execution-isolation","residual_limit":"Isolation limits reachable assets; it does not make injected code trustworthy or rule out a runtime escape.","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Isolate tool execution","verification":"In a test environment, attempt reads outside the workspace, forbidden network connections, and resource exhaustion; retain policy and denial evidence."}],"finding_ids":["592fbfc9b7dab062dc97906c"],"id":"group-0a77dbbc61c4","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Review the effective permission policy and restore bounded tools and runtime isolation; require independent approval for the specific sensitive effects.","locations":[{"end_line":7,"finding_id":"592fbfc9b7dab062dc97906c","line":7,"path":"mcp.json"}],"plausible_impact":"If unrestricted execution or disabled approval is effective, malicious context or an erroneous plan may reach sensitive actions with the agent identity.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI031","severity":"high","source_ids":["ASD-HARNESS","JOINT-DEPLOY","MCP-SECURITY","MCP-TOOLS","OWASP-AGENT-CS","OWASP-LLM2026","OWASP-MCP-CS"],"sources":[{"id":"ASD-HARNESS","title":"Agentic AI harnesses: The layer above the model","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/agentic-ai-harnesses"},{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"MCP-SECURITY","title":"MCP Security Best Practices","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices"},{"id":"MCP-TOOLS","title":"MCP: Tools","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"},{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"},{"id":"OWASP-LLM2026","title":"OWASP GenAI LLM Top 10 2026","url":"https://genai.owasp.org/resource/owasp-genai-llm-top-10-2026/"},{"id":"OWASP-MCP-CS","title":"MCP Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/MCP_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Agent/platform owner","title":"Agent approval or sandbox safeguard explicitly bypassed"},{"confidence_counts":{"high":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["MCP-09","SUP-01"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["SUP-01","SUP-03"],"how_it_helps":"Use a committed lock or approved artifact manifest, enforce it during installation, and retain the resolved dependency inventory.","id":"immutable-install","residual_limit":"An exact version or digest can still identify a vulnerable artifact; mutable transitive dependencies must also be constrained.","source_ids":["NIST-SSDF","OPENSSF-BASELINE-202608"],"sources":[{"id":"NIST-SSDF","title":"Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1","url":"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final"},{"id":"OPENSSF-BASELINE-202608","title":"Open Source Project Security Baseline","url":"https://baseline.openssf.org/versions/2026-08-28"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Resolve and install reviewed dependency bytes","verification":"Build in a clean environment and compare resolved bytes; modify a lock or artifact and verify the release gate rejects it."},{"control_ids":["SUP-03","DATA-04"],"how_it_helps":"Require reviewed artifact provenance plus a digest or signature checked against an independently trusted identity or manifest.","id":"artifact-verification","residual_limit":"Authenticity establishes the producer and bytes; an approved producer can still ship vulnerable or malicious content.","source_ids":["SLSA-12","OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING"],"sources":[{"id":"OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","title":"Launch of Model Signing v1.0","url":"https://openssf.org/blog/2025/04/04/launch-of-model-signing-v1-0-openssf-ai-ml-working-group-secures-the-machine-learning-supply-chain/"},{"id":"SLSA-12","title":"Supply-chain Levels for Software Artifacts specification","url":"https://slsa.dev/spec/v1.2/"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Verify artifact identity before use","verification":"Substitute bytes, producer identity, or verification metadata in a controlled test and confirm the consumer rejects the artifact."},{"control_ids":["AUTH-05","AUTH-09"],"how_it_helps":"Give this component a distinct identity and only the downstream scopes and lifetime needed for its approved operations.","id":"secret-boundary","residual_limit":"A compromised component can still use its allowed permissions until credentials expire or revocation takes effect.","source_ids":["JOINT-AGENTIC"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Limit credentials available to the workload","verification":"Use its runtime identity to attempt forbidden service operations, then revoke it and confirm subsequent access fails."}],"finding_ids":["6b77081a826c4c6833edc47f"],"id":"group-964934e5a62a","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Resolve and approve exact executable and transitive artifacts, enforce the lock at launch, and minimize inherited environment secrets.","locations":[{"end_line":4,"finding_id":"6b77081a826c4c6833edc47f","line":4,"path":"mcp.json"}],"plausible_impact":"If the package runner resolves a changed or malicious artifact, the next MCP launch could execute different code with the client environment permissions.","priority":"P2","rule_id":"AI018","severity":"medium","source_ids":["CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","JOINT-AGENTIC","MCP-SECURITY","NIST-SSDF","OPENSSF-BASELINE-202608","OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","OWASP-MCP-CS","SLSA-12"],"sources":[{"id":"CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","title":"Shifting the Balance of Cybersecurity Risk: Principles and Approaches for Secure by Design Software","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/secure-by-design"},{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"},{"id":"MCP-SECURITY","title":"MCP Security Best Practices","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices"},{"id":"NIST-SSDF","title":"Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1","url":"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final"},{"id":"OPENSSF-BASELINE-202608","title":"Open Source Project Security Baseline","url":"https://baseline.openssf.org/versions/2026-08-28"},{"id":"OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","title":"Launch of Model Signing v1.0","url":"https://openssf.org/blog/2025/04/04/launch-of-model-signing-v1-0-openssf-ai-ml-working-group-secures-the-machine-learning-supply-chain/"},{"id":"OWASP-MCP-CS","title":"MCP Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/MCP_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"},{"id":"SLSA-12","title":"Supply-chain Levels for Software Artifacts specification","url":"https://slsa.dev/spec/v1.2/"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"MCP integration/build owner","title":"MCP package runner resolves an unpinned artifact"},{"confidence_counts":{"high":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["SUP-05"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["SUP-05","TEST-05"],"how_it_helps":"Use a dedicated nonroot identity, minimal capabilities, no privilege escalation, and an enforced syscall and mandatory-access policy where supported.","id":"runtime-restrictions","residual_limit":"Nonroot alone is insufficient; writable mounts, added capabilities, host namespaces, and kernel flaws can weaken isolation.","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY","CIS-CONTROLS-81"],"sources":[{"id":"CIS-CONTROLS-81","title":"CIS Critical Security Controls v8.1","url":"https://www.cisecurity.org/controls/v8-1"},{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Apply runtime isolation controls together","verification":"Inspect the effective workload and attempt privileged operations, prohibited syscalls, and access to protected host resources."},{"control_ids":["SUP-05","TEST-04","GOV-02"],"how_it_helps":"Place tools needing exceptional privileges in a separate environment with narrow interfaces and no unrelated tenant data.","id":"workload-separation","residual_limit":"Shared kernels or administrative infrastructure may retain common failure paths; a container is not automatically a strong hostile-code boundary.","source_ids":["JOINT-AGENTIC","CSA-CCM"],"sources":[{"id":"CSA-CCM","title":"Cloud Controls Matrix and CAIQ v4.1","url":"https://cloudsecurityalliance.org/artifacts/cloud-controls-matrix-v4-1"},{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Separate risky tools from sensitive workloads","verification":"Test cross-workload network and filesystem access and confirm the privileged component cannot impersonate the requesting agent."}],"finding_ids":["20771a324af20de316ec34f9"],"id":"group-f42ebc88841c","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Verify the final build stage and deployed user, then run with a dedicated nonroot identity unless a documented operation requires otherwise.","locations":[{"end_line":3,"finding_id":"20771a324af20de316ec34f9","line":2,"path":"Dockerfile"}],"plausible_impact":"If this is the effective runtime user, a tool compromise may gain more authority within the container; host impact depends on mounts, capabilities, user mappings, and kernel isolation.","priority":"P2","rule_id":"AI021","severity":"medium","source_ids":["CIS-CONTROLS-81","CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","CSA-CCM","JOINT-AGENTIC","JOINT-DEPLOY"],"sources":[{"id":"CIS-CONTROLS-81","title":"CIS Critical Security Controls v8.1","url":"https://www.cisecurity.org/controls/v8-1"},{"id":"CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","title":"Shifting the Balance of Cybersecurity Risk: Principles and Approaches for Secure by Design Software","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/secure-by-design"},{"id":"CSA-CCM","title":"Cloud Controls Matrix and CAIQ v4.1","url":"https://cloudsecurityalliance.org/artifacts/cloud-controls-matrix-v4-1"},{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"},{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Container/platform owner","title":"Container explicitly runs as root"},{"confidence_counts":{"low":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["SUP-01","SUP-03"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["SUP-03","DATA-04"],"how_it_helps":"Require reviewed artifact provenance plus a digest or signature checked against an independently trusted identity or manifest.","id":"artifact-verification","residual_limit":"Authenticity establishes the producer and bytes; an approved producer can still ship vulnerable or malicious content.","source_ids":["SLSA-12","OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING"],"sources":[{"id":"OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","title":"Launch of Model Signing v1.0","url":"https://openssf.org/blog/2025/04/04/launch-of-model-signing-v1-0-openssf-ai-ml-working-group-secures-the-machine-learning-supply-chain/"},{"id":"SLSA-12","title":"Supply-chain Levels for Software Artifacts specification","url":"https://slsa.dev/spec/v1.2/"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Verify artifact identity before use","verification":"Substitute bytes, producer identity, or verification metadata in a controlled test and confirm the consumer rejects the artifact."},{"control_ids":["SUP-02","SUP-04","OPS-05"],"how_it_helps":"Review known-vulnerability and maintenance evidence for the actual resolved artifacts and apply updates through a repeatable release process.","id":"maintenance-loop","residual_limit":"This source/image scan does not provide a current CVE verdict, and a vulnerability database cannot identify every unknown flaw.","source_ids":["NIST-SSDF","OPENSSF-SCORECARD"],"sources":[{"id":"NIST-SSDF","title":"Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1","url":"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final"},{"id":"OPENSSF-SCORECARD","title":"OpenSSF Scorecard","url":"https://securityscorecards.dev/"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Keep pinned artifacts maintained","verification":"Demonstrate a dependency update, relevant regression checks, and deployment or rollback of the resulting approved artifact."}],"finding_ids":["055ed29e5f56926f1827a0b8"],"id":"group-0cc3d39352a0","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Identify the approved image digest and enforce it in the effective build or deployment while preserving a reviewed update process.","locations":[{"end_line":1,"finding_id":"055ed29e5f56926f1827a0b8","line":1,"path":"Dockerfile"}],"plausible_impact":"If a mutable image tag changes, a rebuild or deployment may consume unreviewed bytes; the scan does not establish that the current image is vulnerable.","priority":"P3","rule_id":"AI024","severity":"low","source_ids":["CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","NIST-SSDF","NSA-DATA","OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","OPENSSF-SCORECARD","SLSA-12"],"sources":[{"id":"CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","title":"Shifting the Balance of Cybersecurity Risk: Principles and Approaches for Secure by Design Software","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/secure-by-design"},{"id":"NIST-SSDF","title":"Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1","url":"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final"},{"id":"NSA-DATA","title":"AI Data Security: Best Practices for Securing Data Used to Train & Operate AI Systems (NSA announcement)","url":"https://www.nsa.gov/Press-Room/Press-Releases-Statements/Press-Release-View/Article/4192332/nsas-aisc-releases-joint-guidance-on-the-risks-and-best-practices-in-ai-data-se/"},{"id":"OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","title":"Launch of Model Signing v1.0","url":"https://openssf.org/blog/2025/04/04/launch-of-model-signing-v1-0-openssf-ai-ml-working-group-secures-the-machine-learning-supply-chain/"},{"id":"OPENSSF-SCORECARD","title":"OpenSSF Scorecard","url":"https://securityscorecards.dev/"},{"id":"SLSA-12","title":"Supply-chain Levels for Software Artifacts specification","url":"https://slsa.dev/spec/v1.2/"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Container/release owner","title":"Container image is not digest pinned"}],"guidance":{"catalog_version":"1.0.0","reviewed_at":"2026-09-19","sha256":"dadde42b9b4e7f65d34d897f716649ed0b49b1fc561e5e45a9eadbac43c5eed1","source_registry_sha256":"cb7d62fe5f3b856a424ddc3b7afa986563a48b5ec2104423055a91fe290d5142"},"immediate_actions":[{"confidence_counts":{"medium":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["EXEC-02"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["AGT-01","AUTH-02","MCP-02"],"how_it_helps":"Have an execution service allow only named operations, permitted argument values, and caller-owned target resources before invoking a tool.","id":"tool-policy","residual_limit":"Authorized operations can still be harmful when business constraints are incomplete; prompt instructions cannot enforce this boundary.","source_ids":["OWASP-AGENT-CS","MCP-TOOLS"],"sources":[{"id":"MCP-TOOLS","title":"MCP: Tools","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"},{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Enforce action policy outside the model","verification":"Exercise disallowed operations, additional arguments, cross-tenant identifiers, and direct calls that bypass the agent planner."},{"control_ids":["EXEC-02","SUP-05","OPS-02"],"how_it_helps":"Run the risky tool in a separate, disposable identity with no host mounts, ambient credentials, or unnecessary outbound access.","id":"execution-isolation","residual_limit":"Isolation limits reachable assets; it does not make injected code trustworthy or rule out a runtime escape.","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Isolate tool execution","verification":"In a test environment, attempt reads outside the workspace, forbidden network connections, and resource exhaustion; retain policy and denial evidence."}],"finding_ids":["b1b0f0a3f33fe93875fcb58a"],"id":"group-45290f4fa5c7","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Trace the input to eval/exec and replace it with fixed operations; if generated execution is essential, isolate it before accepting untrusted input.","locations":[{"end_line":16,"finding_id":"b1b0f0a3f33fe93875fcb58a","line":16,"path":"agent.py"}],"plausible_impact":"If external or generated content reaches this expression, it could execute Python with the process identity and access its files, credentials, and network.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI001","severity":"high","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY","MCP-TOOLS","OWASP-AGENT-CS","OWASP-LLM2026","TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"MCP-TOOLS","title":"MCP: Tools","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"},{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"},{"id":"OWASP-LLM2026","title":"OWASP GenAI LLM Top 10 2026","url":"https://genai.owasp.org/resource/owasp-genai-llm-top-10-2026/"},{"id":"TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY","title":"Python Security Considerations","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/security_warnings.html"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Agent/tool developer","title":"Dynamic Python code execution"},{"confidence_counts":{"medium":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["EXEC-01"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["AGT-01","AUTH-02","MCP-02"],"how_it_helps":"Have an execution service allow only named operations, permitted argument values, and caller-owned target resources before invoking a tool.","id":"tool-policy","residual_limit":"Authorized operations can still be harmful when business constraints are incomplete; prompt instructions cannot enforce this boundary.","source_ids":["OWASP-AGENT-CS","MCP-TOOLS"],"sources":[{"id":"MCP-TOOLS","title":"MCP: Tools","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"},{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Enforce action policy outside the model","verification":"Exercise disallowed operations, additional arguments, cross-tenant identifiers, and direct calls that bypass the agent planner."},{"control_ids":["EXEC-02","SUP-05","OPS-02"],"how_it_helps":"Run the risky tool in a separate, disposable identity with no host mounts, ambient credentials, or unnecessary outbound access.","id":"execution-isolation","residual_limit":"Isolation limits reachable assets; it does not make injected code trustworthy or rule out a runtime escape.","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Isolate tool execution","verification":"In a test environment, attempt reads outside the workspace, forbidden network connections, and resource exhaustion; retain policy and denial evidence."}],"finding_ids":["979d192981c1785a2394fe19"],"id":"group-66e04ed7d9ac","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Remove shell interpretation, select a fixed executable, and validate each argument and permitted option.","locations":[{"end_line":9,"finding_id":"979d192981c1785a2394fe19","line":9,"path":"agent.py"}],"plausible_impact":"If a caller or agent controls command content, shell syntax could alter the intended operation and execute with the tool process permissions.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI002","severity":"high","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY","MCP-TOOLS","OWASP-AGENT-CS","OWASP-LLM2026","OWASP-MCP10","OWASP-OUTPUT2025","TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"MCP-TOOLS","title":"MCP: Tools","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"},{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"},{"id":"OWASP-LLM2026","title":"OWASP GenAI LLM Top 10 2026","url":"https://genai.owasp.org/resource/owasp-genai-llm-top-10-2026/"},{"id":"OWASP-MCP10","title":"OWASP MCP Top 10","url":"https://owasp.org/projects/mcp-top-10"},{"id":"OWASP-OUTPUT2025","title":"LLM05:2025 Improper Output Handling","url":"https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm052025-improper-output-handling/"},{"id":"TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY","title":"Python Security Considerations","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/security_warnings.html"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Agent/tool developer","title":"Dynamic command executed through a shell"},{"confidence_counts":{"medium":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["EXEC-01"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["AGT-01","AUTH-02","MCP-02"],"how_it_helps":"Have an execution service allow only named operations, permitted argument values, and caller-owned target resources before invoking a tool.","id":"tool-policy","residual_limit":"Authorized operations can still be harmful when business constraints are incomplete; prompt instructions cannot enforce this boundary.","source_ids":["OWASP-AGENT-CS","MCP-TOOLS"],"sources":[{"id":"MCP-TOOLS","title":"MCP: Tools","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"},{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Enforce action policy outside the model","verification":"Exercise disallowed operations, additional arguments, cross-tenant identifiers, and direct calls that bypass the agent planner."},{"control_ids":["EXEC-02","SUP-05","OPS-02"],"how_it_helps":"Run the risky tool in a separate, disposable identity with no host mounts, ambient credentials, or unnecessary outbound access.","id":"execution-isolation","residual_limit":"Isolation limits reachable assets; it does not make injected code trustworthy or rule out a runtime escape.","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Isolate tool execution","verification":"In a test environment, attempt reads outside the workspace, forbidden network connections, and resource exhaustion; retain policy and denial evidence."}],"finding_ids":["0fa7e450cd583d78646ef397"],"id":"group-f0e53150bfd5","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Replace os.system/os.popen with a fixed executable and validated argument list; trace all contributing values.","locations":[{"end_line":10,"finding_id":"0fa7e450cd583d78646ef397","line":10,"path":"agent.py"}],"plausible_impact":"If external values contribute to the command string, the shell could execute additional commands with the server identity.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI003","severity":"high","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY","MCP-TOOLS","OWASP-AGENT-CS","OWASP-LLM2026","OWASP-MCP10","OWASP-OUTPUT2025","TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"MCP-TOOLS","title":"MCP: Tools","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"},{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"},{"id":"OWASP-LLM2026","title":"OWASP GenAI LLM Top 10 2026","url":"https://genai.owasp.org/resource/owasp-genai-llm-top-10-2026/"},{"id":"OWASP-MCP10","title":"OWASP MCP Top 10","url":"https://owasp.org/projects/mcp-top-10"},{"id":"OWASP-OUTPUT2025","title":"LLM05:2025 Improper Output Handling","url":"https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm052025-improper-output-handling/"},{"id":"TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY","title":"Python Security Considerations","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/security_warnings.html"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Agent/tool developer","title":"Dynamic os shell command"},{"confidence_counts":{"medium":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["EXEC-06"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["SUP-03","DATA-04"],"how_it_helps":"Require reviewed artifact provenance plus a digest or signature checked against an independently trusted identity or manifest.","id":"artifact-verification","residual_limit":"Authenticity establishes the producer and bytes; an approved producer can still ship vulnerable or malicious content.","source_ids":["SLSA-12","OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING"],"sources":[{"id":"OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","title":"Launch of Model Signing v1.0","url":"https://openssf.org/blog/2025/04/04/launch-of-model-signing-v1-0-openssf-ai-ml-working-group-secures-the-machine-learning-supply-chain/"},{"id":"SLSA-12","title":"Supply-chain Levels for Software Artifacts specification","url":"https://slsa.dev/spec/v1.2/"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Verify artifact identity before use","verification":"Substitute bytes, producer identity, or verification metadata in a controlled test and confirm the consumer rejects the artifact."},{"control_ids":["EXEC-06","SUP-06"],"how_it_helps":"Perform necessary conversion of legacy serialized artifacts in a disposable environment without production data or credentials.","id":"isolated-conversion","residual_limit":"Conversion output still needs integrity, format, and downstream behavior review; isolation is not proof of benign content.","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY","TECH-PYTORCH-SERIAL"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"TECH-PYTORCH-SERIAL","title":"PyTorch Serialization semantics","url":"https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/notes/serialization.html"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Separate artifact conversion from production","verification":"Demonstrate that a conversion job cannot reach production services and only approved output formats are promoted."}],"finding_ids":["d2d09fb2875db72f18779bfc"],"id":"group-9ee5075ce1a1","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Establish who can produce and replace the input; migrate to a nonexecutable data format or restrict verified legacy artifacts to an isolated conversion path.","locations":[{"end_line":12,"finding_id":"d2d09fb2875db72f18779bfc","line":12,"path":"agent.py"}],"plausible_impact":"If an attacker can supply or replace the serialized input, loading it may execute code even before the application examines the returned object.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI005","severity":"high","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY","NIST-SSDF","OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","SLSA-12","TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY","TECH-PYTORCH-SERIAL"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"NIST-SSDF","title":"Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1","url":"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final"},{"id":"OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","title":"Launch of Model Signing v1.0","url":"https://openssf.org/blog/2025/04/04/launch-of-model-signing-v1-0-openssf-ai-ml-working-group-secures-the-machine-learning-supply-chain/"},{"id":"SLSA-12","title":"Supply-chain Levels for Software Artifacts specification","url":"https://slsa.dev/spec/v1.2/"},{"id":"TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY","title":"Python Security Considerations","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/security_warnings.html"},{"id":"TECH-PYTORCH-SERIAL","title":"PyTorch Serialization semantics","url":"https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/notes/serialization.html"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Application/model pipeline owner","title":"Executable deserialization requires trusted inputs"},{"confidence_counts":{"high":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["MCP-01"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["MCP-01","AUTH-05"],"how_it_helps":"Use verified TLS on every relevant network hop, with an appropriate public or private CA and validated service hostname.","id":"trusted-transport","residual_limit":"TLS does not protect data from an authorized endpoint, compromised gateway, or plaintext segments beyond termination.","source_ids":["MCP-AUTH","MCP-AUTH-SEC"],"sources":[{"id":"MCP-AUTH","title":"MCP: Authorization","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH-SEC","title":"MCP: Authorization Security Considerations","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization/security-considerations"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Require authenticated encrypted transport","verification":"Present an untrusted, expired, or wrong-host certificate and verify rejection; inspect backend traffic after TLS termination."},{"control_ids":["EXEC-05","AGT-07","SUP-05"],"how_it_helps":"Enforce an outbound policy outside the application that permits only required destinations and services; include IPv6 and proxy paths.","id":"egress-policy","residual_limit":"Allowed destinations may themselves accept leaked data; destination rules do not replace content and action authorization.","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY","MCP-SECURITY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"MCP-SECURITY","title":"MCP Security Best Practices","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Restrict outbound destinations independently","verification":"From the deployed identity, test direct IP, DNS, redirect, metadata-service, and proxy-mediated attempts to prohibited destinations."}],"finding_ids":["07fc5f6fd7699fd0194dc479"],"id":"group-08a6f7f32c94","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Enable certificate and hostname verification; install the intended CA for a private gateway and test rejection of an untrusted certificate.","locations":[{"end_line":11,"finding_id":"07fc5f6fd7699fd0194dc479","line":11,"path":"agent.py"}],"plausible_impact":"If a network intermediary can impersonate the destination, disabled verification may expose or alter credentials, prompts, and tool responses.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI006","severity":"high","source_ids":["CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","JOINT-DEPLOY","MCP-AUTH","MCP-AUTH-SEC","MCP-HTTP","MCP-SECURITY"],"sources":[{"id":"CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","title":"Shifting the Balance of Cybersecurity Risk: Principles and Approaches for Secure by Design Software","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/secure-by-design"},{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH","title":"MCP: Authorization","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH-SEC","title":"MCP: Authorization Security Considerations","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization/security-considerations"},{"id":"MCP-HTTP","title":"MCP: Streamable HTTP transport","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/streamable-http"},{"id":"MCP-SECURITY","title":"MCP Security Best Practices","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Application and gateway owner","title":"TLS certificate verification disabled"},{"confidence_counts":{"medium":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["AUTH-05","DATA-01"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["AUTH-05","OPS-06"],"how_it_helps":"For a real exposed credential, identify reachable systems, revoke or rotate it, and review access records for misuse.","id":"exposure-response","residual_limit":"Successful rotation stops future use of that credential but cannot reverse access or data loss that already occurred.","source_ids":["CISA-JCDC","NIST-SSDF"],"sources":[{"id":"CISA-JCDC","title":"JCDC AI Cybersecurity Collaboration Playbook and Fact Sheet (release notice)","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/alerts/2025/01/14/cisa-releases-jcdc-ai-cybersecurity-collaboration-playbook-and-fact-sheet"},{"id":"NIST-SSDF","title":"Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1","url":"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Investigate and contain confirmed secret exposure","verification":"Confirm the old credential no longer works and record the exposure window, affected copies, and follow-up owner."},{"control_ids":["AUTH-05","DATA-01","DATA-06"],"how_it_helps":"Load secrets at runtime through an approved store or workload identity; keep them out of source, artifacts, and model context.","id":"credential-lifecycle","residual_limit":"Deleting a file or hiding a later image layer does not revoke a credential or erase copies already distributed.","source_ids":["MCP-AUTH","JOINT-AGENTIC"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH","title":"MCP: Authorization","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Use managed credential injection and revocation","verification":"Test rotation and revocation without disclosing values; inspect build layers and launch metadata for retained copies."},{"control_ids":["AUTH-05","AUTH-09"],"how_it_helps":"Give this component a distinct identity and only the downstream scopes and lifetime needed for its approved operations.","id":"secret-boundary","residual_limit":"A compromised component can still use its allowed permissions until credentials expire or revocation takes effect.","source_ids":["JOINT-AGENTIC"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Limit credentials available to the workload","verification":"Use its runtime identity to attempt forbidden service operations, then revoke it and confirm subsequent access fails."}],"finding_ids":["afb2bdb94696690028650faf"],"id":"group-57a1992f928c","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Determine whether the value is real without reproducing it; revoke or rotate a real exposed credential and remove retained copies through the incident process.","locations":[{"end_line":6,"finding_id":"afb2bdb94696690028650faf","line":6,"path":"mcp.json"}],"plausible_impact":"If the detected literal is a live credential, anyone with access to the source, image layers, or copied artifacts may use its granted permissions.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI010","severity":"high","source_ids":["CISA-JCDC","CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","JOINT-AGENTIC","JOINT-DEPLOY","MCP-AUTH","MCP-AUTH-SEC","MCP-SECURITY","NIST-SSDF"],"sources":[{"id":"CISA-JCDC","title":"JCDC AI Cybersecurity Collaboration Playbook and Fact Sheet (release notice)","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/alerts/2025/01/14/cisa-releases-jcdc-ai-cybersecurity-collaboration-playbook-and-fact-sheet"},{"id":"CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","title":"Shifting the Balance of Cybersecurity Risk: Principles and Approaches for Secure by Design Software","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/secure-by-design"},{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"},{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH","title":"MCP: Authorization","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH-SEC","title":"MCP: Authorization Security Considerations","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization/security-considerations"},{"id":"MCP-SECURITY","title":"MCP Security Best Practices","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices"},{"id":"NIST-SSDF","title":"Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1","url":"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Credential/service owner","title":"Credential-like literal in source or configuration"},{"confidence_counts":{"high":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["MCP-01"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["MCP-01","AUTH-05"],"how_it_helps":"Use verified TLS on every relevant network hop, with an appropriate public or private CA and validated service hostname.","id":"trusted-transport","residual_limit":"TLS does not protect data from an authorized endpoint, compromised gateway, or plaintext segments beyond termination.","source_ids":["MCP-AUTH","MCP-AUTH-SEC"],"sources":[{"id":"MCP-AUTH","title":"MCP: Authorization","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH-SEC","title":"MCP: Authorization Security Considerations","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization/security-considerations"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Require authenticated encrypted transport","verification":"Present an untrusted, expired, or wrong-host certificate and verify rejection; inspect backend traffic after TLS termination."},{"control_ids":["AUTH-05","AUTH-09"],"how_it_helps":"Give this component a distinct identity and only the downstream scopes and lifetime needed for its approved operations.","id":"secret-boundary","residual_limit":"A compromised component can still use its allowed permissions until credentials expire or revocation takes effect.","source_ids":["JOINT-AGENTIC"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Limit credentials available to the workload","verification":"Use its runtime identity to attempt forbidden service operations, then revoke it and confirm subsequent access fails."}],"finding_ids":["d841174f55e032505f8136b9"],"id":"group-b69c379f05c4","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Use HTTPS with verified certificates; if a separate protected transport is intentional, document and test every network hop and termination boundary.","locations":[{"end_line":10,"finding_id":"d841174f55e032505f8136b9","line":10,"path":"mcp.json"}],"plausible_impact":"If remote traffic traverses an unprotected link, observers or intermediaries may read or modify MCP credentials, requests, and responses.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI029","severity":"high","source_ids":["JOINT-AGENTIC","MCP-AUTH","MCP-AUTH-SEC","MCP-HTTP","MCP-SECURITY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH","title":"MCP: Authorization","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization"},{"id":"MCP-AUTH-SEC","title":"MCP: Authorization Security Considerations","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization/security-considerations"},{"id":"MCP-HTTP","title":"MCP: Streamable HTTP transport","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/streamable-http"},{"id":"MCP-SECURITY","title":"MCP Security Best Practices","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"MCP/gateway owner","title":"Remote MCP URL uses plaintext HTTP"},{"confidence_counts":{"high":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["AGT-01","AGT-02","MCP-09","SUP-05"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["AGT-01","AUTH-02","MCP-02"],"how_it_helps":"Have an execution service allow only named operations, permitted argument values, and caller-owned target resources before invoking a tool.","id":"tool-policy","residual_limit":"Authorized operations can still be harmful when business constraints are incomplete; prompt instructions cannot enforce this boundary.","source_ids":["OWASP-AGENT-CS","MCP-TOOLS"],"sources":[{"id":"MCP-TOOLS","title":"MCP: Tools","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"},{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Enforce action policy outside the model","verification":"Exercise disallowed operations, additional arguments, cross-tenant identifiers, and direct calls that bypass the agent planner."},{"control_ids":["AGT-02","OPS-04"],"how_it_helps":"Require an independent approval for the exact actor, tool, normalized arguments, target, and expiry before irreversible effects occur.","id":"action-approval","residual_limit":"Approval cannot compensate for misleading previews, excessive approver authority, or actions that happen before the check.","source_ids":["OWASP-AGENT-CS"],"sources":[{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Bind sensitive actions to explicit approval","verification":"Change arguments after approval, replay the approval, and call after expiry; each attempt must be denied before a side effect."},{"control_ids":["EXEC-02","SUP-05","OPS-02"],"how_it_helps":"Run the risky tool in a separate, disposable identity with no host mounts, ambient credentials, or unnecessary outbound access.","id":"execution-isolation","residual_limit":"Isolation limits reachable assets; it does not make injected code trustworthy or rule out a runtime escape.","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Isolate tool execution","verification":"In a test environment, attempt reads outside the workspace, forbidden network connections, and resource exhaustion; retain policy and denial evidence."}],"finding_ids":["592fbfc9b7dab062dc97906c"],"id":"group-0a77dbbc61c4","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Review the effective permission policy and restore bounded tools and runtime isolation; require independent approval for the specific sensitive effects.","locations":[{"end_line":7,"finding_id":"592fbfc9b7dab062dc97906c","line":7,"path":"mcp.json"}],"plausible_impact":"If unrestricted execution or disabled approval is effective, malicious context or an erroneous plan may reach sensitive actions with the agent identity.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI031","severity":"high","source_ids":["ASD-HARNESS","JOINT-DEPLOY","MCP-SECURITY","MCP-TOOLS","OWASP-AGENT-CS","OWASP-LLM2026","OWASP-MCP-CS"],"sources":[{"id":"ASD-HARNESS","title":"Agentic AI harnesses: The layer above the model","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/agentic-ai-harnesses"},{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"MCP-SECURITY","title":"MCP Security Best Practices","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices"},{"id":"MCP-TOOLS","title":"MCP: Tools","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"},{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title":"AI Agent Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"},{"id":"OWASP-LLM2026","title":"OWASP GenAI LLM Top 10 2026","url":"https://genai.owasp.org/resource/owasp-genai-llm-top-10-2026/"},{"id":"OWASP-MCP-CS","title":"MCP Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/MCP_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Agent/platform owner","title":"Agent approval or sandbox safeguard explicitly bypassed"},{"confidence_counts":{"high":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["MCP-09","SUP-01"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["SUP-01","SUP-03"],"how_it_helps":"Use a committed lock or approved artifact manifest, enforce it during installation, and retain the resolved dependency inventory.","id":"immutable-install","residual_limit":"An exact version or digest can still identify a vulnerable artifact; mutable transitive dependencies must also be constrained.","source_ids":["NIST-SSDF","OPENSSF-BASELINE-202608"],"sources":[{"id":"NIST-SSDF","title":"Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1","url":"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final"},{"id":"OPENSSF-BASELINE-202608","title":"Open Source Project Security Baseline","url":"https://baseline.openssf.org/versions/2026-08-28"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Resolve and install reviewed dependency bytes","verification":"Build in a clean environment and compare resolved bytes; modify a lock or artifact and verify the release gate rejects it."},{"control_ids":["SUP-03","DATA-04"],"how_it_helps":"Require reviewed artifact provenance plus a digest or signature checked against an independently trusted identity or manifest.","id":"artifact-verification","residual_limit":"Authenticity establishes the producer and bytes; an approved producer can still ship vulnerable or malicious content.","source_ids":["SLSA-12","OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING"],"sources":[{"id":"OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","title":"Launch of Model Signing v1.0","url":"https://openssf.org/blog/2025/04/04/launch-of-model-signing-v1-0-openssf-ai-ml-working-group-secures-the-machine-learning-supply-chain/"},{"id":"SLSA-12","title":"Supply-chain Levels for Software Artifacts specification","url":"https://slsa.dev/spec/v1.2/"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Verify artifact identity before use","verification":"Substitute bytes, producer identity, or verification metadata in a controlled test and confirm the consumer rejects the artifact."},{"control_ids":["AUTH-05","AUTH-09"],"how_it_helps":"Give this component a distinct identity and only the downstream scopes and lifetime needed for its approved operations.","id":"secret-boundary","residual_limit":"A compromised component can still use its allowed permissions until credentials expire or revocation takes effect.","source_ids":["JOINT-AGENTIC"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Limit credentials available to the workload","verification":"Use its runtime identity to attempt forbidden service operations, then revoke it and confirm subsequent access fails."}],"finding_ids":["6b77081a826c4c6833edc47f"],"id":"group-964934e5a62a","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Resolve and approve exact executable and transitive artifacts, enforce the lock at launch, and minimize inherited environment secrets.","locations":[{"end_line":4,"finding_id":"6b77081a826c4c6833edc47f","line":4,"path":"mcp.json"}],"plausible_impact":"If the package runner resolves a changed or malicious artifact, the next MCP launch could execute different code with the client environment permissions.","priority":"P2","rule_id":"AI018","severity":"medium","source_ids":["CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","JOINT-AGENTIC","MCP-SECURITY","NIST-SSDF","OPENSSF-BASELINE-202608","OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","OWASP-MCP-CS","SLSA-12"],"sources":[{"id":"CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","title":"Shifting the Balance of Cybersecurity Risk: Principles and Approaches for Secure by Design Software","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/secure-by-design"},{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"},{"id":"MCP-SECURITY","title":"MCP Security Best Practices","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices"},{"id":"NIST-SSDF","title":"Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1","url":"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final"},{"id":"OPENSSF-BASELINE-202608","title":"Open Source Project Security Baseline","url":"https://baseline.openssf.org/versions/2026-08-28"},{"id":"OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","title":"Launch of Model Signing v1.0","url":"https://openssf.org/blog/2025/04/04/launch-of-model-signing-v1-0-openssf-ai-ml-working-group-secures-the-machine-learning-supply-chain/"},{"id":"OWASP-MCP-CS","title":"MCP Security Cheat Sheet","url":"https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/MCP_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"},{"id":"SLSA-12","title":"Supply-chain Levels for Software Artifacts specification","url":"https://slsa.dev/spec/v1.2/"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"MCP integration/build owner","title":"MCP package runner resolves an unpinned artifact"},{"confidence_counts":{"high":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["SUP-05"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["SUP-05","TEST-05"],"how_it_helps":"Use a dedicated nonroot identity, minimal capabilities, no privilege escalation, and an enforced syscall and mandatory-access policy where supported.","id":"runtime-restrictions","residual_limit":"Nonroot alone is insufficient; writable mounts, added capabilities, host namespaces, and kernel flaws can weaken isolation.","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY","CIS-CONTROLS-81"],"sources":[{"id":"CIS-CONTROLS-81","title":"CIS Critical Security Controls v8.1","url":"https://www.cisecurity.org/controls/v8-1"},{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Apply runtime isolation controls together","verification":"Inspect the effective workload and attempt privileged operations, prohibited syscalls, and access to protected host resources."},{"control_ids":["SUP-05","TEST-04","GOV-02"],"how_it_helps":"Place tools needing exceptional privileges in a separate environment with narrow interfaces and no unrelated tenant data.","id":"workload-separation","residual_limit":"Shared kernels or administrative infrastructure may retain common failure paths; a container is not automatically a strong hostile-code boundary.","source_ids":["JOINT-AGENTIC","CSA-CCM"],"sources":[{"id":"CSA-CCM","title":"Cloud Controls Matrix and CAIQ v4.1","url":"https://cloudsecurityalliance.org/artifacts/cloud-controls-matrix-v4-1"},{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Separate risky tools from sensitive workloads","verification":"Test cross-workload network and filesystem access and confirm the privileged component cannot impersonate the requesting agent."}],"finding_ids":["20771a324af20de316ec34f9"],"id":"group-f42ebc88841c","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Verify the final build stage and deployed user, then run with a dedicated nonroot identity unless a documented operation requires otherwise.","locations":[{"end_line":3,"finding_id":"20771a324af20de316ec34f9","line":2,"path":"Dockerfile"}],"plausible_impact":"If this is the effective runtime user, a tool compromise may gain more authority within the container; host impact depends on mounts, capabilities, user mappings, and kernel isolation.","priority":"P2","rule_id":"AI021","severity":"medium","source_ids":["CIS-CONTROLS-81","CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","CSA-CCM","JOINT-AGENTIC","JOINT-DEPLOY"],"sources":[{"id":"CIS-CONTROLS-81","title":"CIS Critical Security Controls v8.1","url":"https://www.cisecurity.org/controls/v8-1"},{"id":"CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","title":"Shifting the Balance of Cybersecurity Risk: Principles and Approaches for Secure by Design Software","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/secure-by-design"},{"id":"CSA-CCM","title":"Cloud Controls Matrix and CAIQ v4.1","url":"https://cloudsecurityalliance.org/artifacts/cloud-controls-matrix-v4-1"},{"id":"JOINT-AGENTIC","title":"Careful adoption of agentic AI services","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"},{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Container/platform owner","title":"Container explicitly runs as root"},{"confidence_counts":{"low":1},"context_note":"Source evidence: deployment reachability and active use have not been established.","control_ids":["SUP-01","SUP-03"],"count":1,"defense_layers":[{"control_ids":["SUP-03","DATA-04"],"how_it_helps":"Require reviewed artifact provenance plus a digest or signature checked against an independently trusted identity or manifest.","id":"artifact-verification","residual_limit":"Authenticity establishes the producer and bytes; an approved producer can still ship vulnerable or malicious content.","source_ids":["SLSA-12","OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING"],"sources":[{"id":"OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","title":"Launch of Model Signing v1.0","url":"https://openssf.org/blog/2025/04/04/launch-of-model-signing-v1-0-openssf-ai-ml-working-group-secures-the-machine-learning-supply-chain/"},{"id":"SLSA-12","title":"Supply-chain Levels for Software Artifacts specification","url":"https://slsa.dev/spec/v1.2/"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Verify artifact identity before use","verification":"Substitute bytes, producer identity, or verification metadata in a controlled test and confirm the consumer rejects the artifact."},{"control_ids":["SUP-02","SUP-04","OPS-05"],"how_it_helps":"Review known-vulnerability and maintenance evidence for the actual resolved artifacts and apply updates through a repeatable release process.","id":"maintenance-loop","residual_limit":"This source/image scan does not provide a current CVE verdict, and a vulnerability database cannot identify every unknown flaw.","source_ids":["NIST-SSDF","OPENSSF-SCORECARD"],"sources":[{"id":"NIST-SSDF","title":"Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1","url":"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final"},{"id":"OPENSSF-SCORECARD","title":"OpenSSF Scorecard","url":"https://securityscorecards.dev/"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Keep pinned artifacts maintained","verification":"Demonstrate a dependency update, relevant regression checks, and deployment or rollback of the resulting approved artifact."}],"finding_ids":["055ed29e5f56926f1827a0b8"],"id":"group-0cc3d39352a0","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Identify the approved image digest and enforce it in the effective build or deployment while preserving a reviewed update process.","locations":[{"end_line":1,"finding_id":"055ed29e5f56926f1827a0b8","line":1,"path":"Dockerfile"}],"plausible_impact":"If a mutable image tag changes, a rebuild or deployment may consume unreviewed bytes; the scan does not establish that the current image is vulnerable.","priority":"P3","rule_id":"AI024","severity":"low","source_ids":["CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","NIST-SSDF","NSA-DATA","OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","OPENSSF-SCORECARD","SLSA-12"],"sources":[{"id":"CISA-SECURE-BY-DESIGN","title":"Shifting the Balance of Cybersecurity Risk: Principles and Approaches for Secure by Design Software","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/secure-by-design"},{"id":"NIST-SSDF","title":"Secure Software Development Framework (SSDF) Version 1.1","url":"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final"},{"id":"NSA-DATA","title":"AI Data Security: Best Practices for Securing Data Used to Train & Operate AI Systems (NSA announcement)","url":"https://www.nsa.gov/Press-Room/Press-Releases-Statements/Press-Release-View/Article/4192332/nsas-aisc-releases-joint-guidance-on-the-risks-and-best-practices-in-ai-data-se/"},{"id":"OPENSSF-MODEL-SIGNING","title":"Launch of Model Signing v1.0","url":"https://openssf.org/blog/2025/04/04/launch-of-model-signing-v1-0-openssf-ai-ml-working-group-secures-the-machine-learning-supply-chain/"},{"id":"OPENSSF-SCORECARD","title":"OpenSSF Scorecard","url":"https://securityscorecards.dev/"},{"id":"SLSA-12","title":"Supply-chain Levels for Software Artifacts specification","url":"https://slsa.dev/spec/v1.2/"}],"status":"open","suggested_owner":"Container/release owner","title":"Container image is not digest pinned"}],"method":"deterministic_guidance","metrics":{"active_checks":132,"active_rules":42,"affected_files":3,"checks_total":132,"controls_requiring_validation":66,"controls_total":66,"coverage_gaps":0,"disabled_checks":0,"disabled_controls":0,"disabled_findings":0,"disabled_rules":0,"excluded_controls":0,"files_scanned":3,"justified_checks":0,"justified_controls":0,"justified_findings":0,"justified_rules":0,"mixed_excluded_controls":0,"open_findings":11,"suppressed_findings":0,"urgent_findings":8},"posture":{"code":"urgent_review","explanation":"The scanner found 8 open critical/high patterns among 11 open findings. Confirm exposure and prioritize the actions below. Detector severity is not proof of exploitability or deployed risk.","title":"Critical/high findings need prompt review"},"priority_basis":"P0: critical, P1: high, P2: medium, P3: low/info. These are deterministic review priorities based on detector severity, not incident confirmation, remediation SLAs, likelihood estimates, or residual-risk scores. Confidence describes the detected pattern; applicability must be checked.","schema_version":"1.0","themes":[{"category":"tool_execution","name":"Tool execution","open_findings":3,"rule_ids":["AI001","AI002","AI003"]},{"category":"supply_chain","name":"Supply chain","open_findings":2,"rule_ids":["AI018","AI024"]},{"category":"transport_security","name":"Transport security","open_findings":2,"rule_ids":["AI006","AI029"]},{"category":"agent_permissions","name":"Agent permissions","open_findings":1,"rule_ids":["AI031"]},{"category":"deserialization","name":"Deserialization","open_findings":1,"rule_ids":["AI005"]},{"category":"sandboxing","name":"Sandboxing","open_findings":1,"rule_ids":["AI021"]},{"category":"secrets","name":"Secrets","open_findings":1,"rule_ids":["AI010"]}],"unknowns":["Actual reachability, deployment configuration, upstream validation, data sensitivity, and exploitability require verification.","Authentication, authorization, tenant isolation, tool approvals, prompt-injection resistance, and recovery need runtime or human evidence.","Suggested defense layers have not been verified as deployed. There is no calculated residual-risk score or automatic severity reduction.","No dependency CVE feed or live adversarial agent/MCP benchmark was run. Excluded and unsupported files remain outside the selected scope."]},"configuration":{"default_excluded_directories":[".cache",".git",".hg",".mypy_cache",".next",".pytest_cache",".svn",".tox",".venv","__pycache__","build","coverage","dist","node_modules","vendor","venv"],"exclude":[],"explicit_exclusion_identity_scope":"Existing selected files and directories, including case aliases and file hardlinks; inputs must remain stable during the scan. Device/inode identities are not persisted in reports.","explicit_exclusion_matching":"resolved_paths_and_snapshot_filesystem_identities","generated_outputs_and_judge_config_excluded":true,"max_entries":100000,"max_file_bytes":1000000,"max_files":20000,"max_total_bytes":50000000},"controls":[{"alignment_source_ids":["CSA-AICM","CSA-AISMM","CIS-AGENTS-2026","CIS-MCP-2026"],"assurance":"Not established by this static scan","automated_rule_ids":[],"category":"Governance","checks":["Record owner, deployment, model/version, MCP transport/version, exposed tools, data classes, and external endpoints.","Reconcile approved inventory with deployed configurations; investigate unregistered agents and servers."],"finding_ids":[],"id":"GOV-01","source_ids":["NIST-RMF"],"sources":["https://www.nist.gov/publications/artificial-intelligence-risk-management-framework-ai-rmf-10"],"status":"manual_review_required","suppressed_finding_ids":[],"title":"Inventory every agent, MCP server, tool, and model","validation":"manual"},{"alignment_source_ids":["CSA-MAESTRO","MITRE-ATLAS-202609"],"assurance":"Not established by this static scan","automated_rule_ids":[],"category":"Governance","checks":["Diagram user, model, memory, tool, server, gateway, and downstream service boundaries with their credentials.","Identify who controls each input and the highest-impact action reachable if that input is malicious."],"finding_ids":[],"id":"GOV-02","source_ids":["MITRE-ATLAS","NIST-AML"],"sources":["https://github.com/mitre-atlas/atlas-data","https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/ai/100/2/e2025/final"],"status":"manual_review_required","suppressed_finding_ids":[],"title":"Model trust boundaries and attack paths","validation":"manual"},{"alignment_source_ids":["CSA-AICM","CSA-SCOPING","CSA-AISMM","AIUC1-Q3-2026"],"assurance":"Not established by this static scan","automated_rule_ids":[],"category":"Governance","checks":["Assign an owner to each autonomous action and document permitted purposes, forbidden outcomes, and escalation routes.","Record impact, reversibility, approval requirements, and accepted residual risk before production use."],"finding_ids":[],"id":"GOV-03","source_ids":["NIST-RMF","JOINT-AGENTIC"],"sources":["https://www.nist.gov/publications/artificial-intelligence-risk-management-framework-ai-rmf-10","https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services"],"status":"manual_review_required","suppressed_finding_ids":[],"title":"Define authorized use and accountable owners","validation":"manual"},{"alignment_source_ids":["CSA-AICM","CSA-AISMM","NIST-SSDF-AI"],"assurance":"Not established by this static scan","automated_rule_ids":[],"category":"Governance","checks":["Give each control an owner, evidence link, validation date, result, and next review date.","Time-limit exceptions and require a compensating control; distinguish untested behavior from demonstrated failure."],"finding_ids":[],"id":"GOV-04","source_ids":["NIST-GENAI","NIST-SSDF"],"sources":["https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/ai/NIST.AI.600-1.pdf","https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final"],"status":"manual_review_required","suppressed_finding_ids":[],"title":"Maintain evidence and risk exceptions","validation":"manual"},{"alignment_source_ids":["CSA-AICM","CSA-SCOPING"],"assurance":"Not established by this static scan","automated_rule_ids":[],"category":"Governance","checks":["Review security impact when adding a model, tool, server, data source, skill, or broader permission.","Require deployment evidence for the complete configured system; a model-only score is insufficient."],"finding_ids":[],"id":"GOV-05","source_ids":["NCSC-SECURE-AI"],"sources":["https://www.ncsc.gov.uk/collection/guidelines-secure-ai-system-development"],"status":"manual_review_required","suppressed_finding_ids":[],"title":"Reassess changes in autonomy and integrations","validation":"manual"},{"alignment_source_ids":[],"assurance":"Not established by this static scan","automated_rule_ids":[],"category":"Governance","checks":["For each model, gateway, orchestrator, MCP service, and cloud provider, document which party implements each applicable safeguard and which customer configuration it depends on.","Obtain current supplier evidence for inherited safeguards, identify unowned gaps, and record reassessment triggers in the service review."],"finding_ids":[],"id":"GOV-06","source_ids":["CSA-AICM","CSA-CCM"],"sources":["https://cloudsecurityalliance.org/artifacts/ai-controls-matrix-v1-1","https://cloudsecurityalliance.org/artifacts/cloud-controls-matrix-v4-1"],"status":"manual_review_required","suppressed_finding_ids":[],"title":"Assign shared security responsibilities across AI providers","validation":"manual"},{"alignment_source_ids":["CSA-AGENT-IAM","CIS-MCP-2026","OWASP-AISVS-C10"],"assurance":"Partial static coverage only; absence of a finding is not a pass","automated_rule_ids":["AI026","AI041"],"category":"Identity and authorization","checks":["Trace authentication to every protected HTTP entry point, including tool calls, subscriptions, and retries.","Verify missing, expired, revoked, or malformed credentials cannot invoke a protected operation."],"finding_ids":[],"id":"AUTH-01","source_ids":["MCP-AUTH"],"sources":["https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization"],"status":"no_pattern_detected","suppressed_finding_ids":[],"title":"Authenticate protected operations on every request","validation":"hybrid"},{"alignment_source_ids":["CSA-AICM","CSA-AGENT-IAM","CSA-SCOPING","CIS-MCP-2026","OWASP-AISVS-C9","OWASP-AISVS-C10"],"assurance":"Partial static coverage only; absence of a finding is not a pass","automated_rule_ids":["AI027"],"category":"Identity and authorization","checks":["Check user/agent identity, tenant, tool, target object, and requested operation immediately before execution.","Deny by default; test read-only callers against write tools and object identifiers owned by another user."],"finding_ids":[],"id":"AUTH-02","source_ids":["JOINT-AGENTIC","MCP-TOOLS"],"sources":["https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/careful-adoption-of-agentic-ai-services","https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"],"status":"no_pattern_detected","suppressed_finding_ids":[],"title":"Authorize the exact action and target","validation":"hybrid"},{"alignment_source_ids":["CIS-MCP-2026","OWASP-AISVS-C10"],"assurance":"Partial static coverage only; absence of a finding is not a pass","automated_rule_ids":["AI017"],"category":"Identity and authorization","checks":["Verify signature with trusted keys, allowed algorithms, expected issuer/audience, expiry, and required scopes.","Reject unsigned tokens and tokens minted for another service; decoding a JWT alone is not validation."],"finding_ids":[],"id":"AUTH-03","source_ids":["MCP-AUTH-SEC"],"sources":["https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization/security-considerations"],"status":"no_pattern_detected","suppressed_finding_ids":[],"title":"Validate access-token cryptography and claims","validation":"hybrid"},{"alignment_source_ids":["CIS-MCP-2026","OWASP-AISVS-C10"],"assurance":"Partial static coverage only; absence of a finding is not a pass","automated_rule_ids":["AI028"],"category":"Identity and authorization","checks":["Use audience-bound MCP credentials and separately authorized downstream credentials; never forward arbitrary caller tokens.","Ensure a proxy cannot use its broader service identity to perform an action the caller cannot authorize."],"finding_ids":[],"id":"AUTH-04","source_ids":["MCP-AUTH","MCP-SECURITY"],"sources":["https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization","https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices"],"status":"no_pattern_detected","suppressed_finding_ids":[],"title":"Prevent token passthrough and confused deputy use","validation":"hybrid"},{"alignment_source_ids":["CSA-AGENT-IAM","CIS-AGENTS-2026","CIS-MCP-2026","OWASP-AISVS-C9"],"assurance":"Partial static coverage only; absence of a finding is not a pass","automated_rule_ids":["AI010","AI011","AI030","AI034"],"category":"Identity and authorization","checks":["Use short-lived scoped credentials where supported, protect refresh tokens, and validate rotation and revocation.","Avoid tokens in query strings, model context, source, child-process arguments, and diagnostic output."],"finding_ids":["afb2bdb94696690028650faf"],"id":"AUTH-05","source_ids":["MCP-AUTH-SEC","JOINT-DEPLOY"],"sources":["https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization/security-considerations","https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"],"status":"findings_detected","suppressed_finding_ids":[],"title":"Constrain credential lifetime and exposure","validation":"hybrid"},{"alignment_source_ids":[],"assurance":"Partial static coverage only; absence of a finding is not a pass","automated_rule_ids":["AI038"],"category":"Identity and authorization","checks":["Test PKCE support and S256, exact registered redirects, transaction binding, and authorization-response issuer validation.","Reject replayed codes, mismatched issuers, unsafe redirect schemes, and unsolicited callback transactions."],"finding_ids":[],"id":"AUTH-06","source_ids":["MCP-AUTH-SEC","MCP-AUTH"],"sources":["https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization/security-considerations","https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization"],"status":"no_pattern_detected","suppressed_finding_ids":[],"title":"Bind OAuth flows and validate redirects","validation":"hybrid"},{"alignment_source_ids":[],"assurance":"Not established by this static scan","automated_rule_ids":[],"category":"Identity and authorization","checks":["Validate discovered metadata and client metadata URLs before fetching; constrain schemes, destinations, redirects, and response sizes.","Document trust policy for client registration and prevent discovery from reaching internal metadata or privileged network services."],"finding_ids":[],"id":"AUTH-07","source_ids":["MCP-SECURITY"],"sources":["https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices"],"status":"review_required","suppressed_finding_ids":[],"title":"Secure OAuth discovery and registration","validation":"hybrid"},{"alignment_source_ids":["CSA-AGENT-IAM","NIST-AGENT-IDENTITY-DRAFT","CIS-AGENTS-2026","CIS-MCP-2026","OWASP-AISVS-C9"],"assurance":"Not established by this static scan","automated_rule_ids":[],"category":"Identity and authorization","checks":["Carry authenticated initiator and delegation identity through multi-agent calls instead of trusting identity fields in text.","Prevent agents from granting themselves privileges; limit delegation scope, depth, lifetime, and downstream audiences."],"finding_ids":[],"id":"AUTH-08","source_ids":["OWASP-AGENT-CS"],"sources":["https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"],"status":"review_required","suppressed_finding_ids":[],"title":"Bind delegation to identity, scope, and expiry","validation":"hybrid"},{"alignment_source_ids":[],"assurance":"Not established by this static scan","automated_rule_ids":[],"category":"Identity and authorization","checks":["Enroll agents under an accountable sponsor and approved workload identity; verify identity claims before issuing credentials or granting discovery and execution access.","Test retirement, sponsor departure, redeployment, and identity compromise; remove stale credentials, cached grants, registrations, and downstream access."],"finding_ids":[],"id":"AUTH-09","source_ids":["CSA-AGENT-IAM","NIST-AGENT-IDENTITY-DRAFT"],"sources":["https://cloudsecurityalliance.org/artifacts/agentic-ai-identity-and-access-management-a-new-approach","https://www.nccoe.nist.gov/publications/other/accelerating-adoption-software-and-ai-agent-identity-and-authorization-concept"],"status":"runtime_validation_required","suppressed_finding_ids":[],"title":"Manage agent identity enrollment and retirement","validation":"dynamic"},{"alignment_source_ids":["OWASP-AISVS-C10"],"assurance":"Partial static coverage only; absence of a finding is not a pass","automated_rule_ids":["AI006","AI007","AI008","AI029"],"category":"MCP protocol and tools","checks":["For HTTP, reject invalid Origin values and verify local deployments bind only to intended interfaces.","Use TLS for remote protected endpoints; test DNS rebinding and proxy/header behavior in deployment."],"finding_ids":["07fc5f6fd7699fd0194dc479","d841174f55e032505f8136b9"],"id":"MCP-01","source_ids":["MCP-HTTP"],"sources":["https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/streamable-http"],"status":"findings_detected","suppressed_finding_ids":[],"title":"Validate transport exposure and origin","validation":"hybrid"},{"alignment_source_ids":["CIS-MCP-2026","OWASP-AISVS-C9","OWASP-AISVS-C10"],"assurance":"Not established by this static scan","automated_rule_ids":[],"category":"MCP protocol and tools","checks":["Apply schemas and semantic bounds before executing every tool; reject unknown properties where appropriate.","Bound sizes and nesting; validate declared structured output and render errors without leaking secrets."],"finding_ids":[],"id":"MCP-02","source_ids":["MCP-TOOLS"],"sources":["https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"],"status":"review_required","suppressed_finding_ids":[],"title":"Validate tool arguments and results","validation":"hybrid"},{"alignment_source_ids":["OWASP-AISVS-C10"],"assurance":"Not established by this static scan","automated_rule_ids":[],"category":"MCP protocol and tools","checks":["Inspect descriptions, schemas, resources, icons, and results for instructions that cross tool or user boundaries.","Never let readOnlyHint, destructiveHint, or other server claims replace independent authorization and approval policy."],"finding_ids":[],"id":"MCP-03","source_ids":["MCP-TOOLS","OWASP-MCP-CS"],"sources":["https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools","https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/MCP_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html"],"status":"review_required","suppressed_finding_ids":[],"title":"Treat descriptions and annotations as untrusted","validation":"hybrid"},{"alignment_source_ids":["OWASP-AISVS-C10"],"assurance":"Not established by this static scan","automated_rule_ids":[],"category":"MCP protocol 